    "type": "tenant-isolation",
    "priority": 1,
    "passes": true,
    "notes": "Tenant isolation for quota_reservations. Implemented internal/controlplane/store/quota_reservation_tenant_isolation_test.go covering 7 cross-tenant invariants on the QuotaRepository reservation surface: (1) InsertReservation cross-tenant bystander byte-identity — orgA's InsertReservation for the SAME resource orgB already owns on (active and committed peers across services/projects/databases) leaves every observable column on every orgB row byte-identical (id, organization_id, resource, amount, status, job_id, expires_at, settled_at, created_at, updated_at — updated_at is the load-bearing trigger anchor via quota_reservations_set_updated_at BEFORE UPDATE); (2) cross-tenant row-count invariant — orgA's InsertReservation on a resource orgB has not seeded changes orgA's count by +1 and leaves orgB's count untouched; (3) same-resource-and-amount in two tenants both persist as the positive-direction pair (no UNIQUE on (organization_id, resource); only PRIMARY KEY (id) and UNIQUE (organization_id, id) composite-FK target) — without this pair a regression resolving a phantom conflict by (resource,) alone would prevent orgA's INSERT and the bystander assertions above would silently pass against unmutated rows; (4) global PRIMARY KEY collision across tenants surfaces as typed apierr.Conflict (yerr.CodeConflict) through mapWriteError AND leaves orgB's row byte-identical AND inserts no orgA row — a cross-tenant requester cannot UPDATE orgB's row through an explicit-id collision; (5) SumActiveReservations tenant-scoping — orgA's sum on services = orgA totals only, orgB's sum on services = orgB totals only, even when both tenants hold rows on the same resource (10 vs 300 chosen so a cross-tenant fold would surface as 310); the orthogonal projects peer also guards the resource predicate; (6) SumActiveReservations on empty tenant returns 0 even when other tenants hold many rows on the same resource — defensive proof the organization_id predicate keeps cross-tenant rows out of the SUM source set; (7) ON DELETE CASCADE tenant isolation — deleting orgA via raw SQL CASCADE-removes orgA's quota_reservations rows and leaves orgB's three peers (active services, active projects, committed databases) byte-identical to baseline, mirroring TestQuotaUsageOrganizationDeleteCascadeIsTenantScoped (BE-0454). Helpers introduced: assertQuotaReservationByteIdentical + per-file ptr helpers stringPtrEqualQR/timePtrEqualQR/fmtStringPtrQR/fmtTimePtrQR (per-file QR suffix is mandatory because the package-shared store_test space already exposes QP-suffixed variants from BE-0451). All other helpers reused: seedOrg (schema_test.go), insertReservationRow/insertSettledReservationRow (quota_repository_test.go), loadQuotaReservationRowByID/countQuotaReservationRowsForOrg/runInsertReservationOrFail (BE-0455 invariants). All 7 tests PASS against an isolated migrated Postgres (race-clean, 2.83s). gofmt/vet clean. Pre-existing TestEnvironmentService*, TestAPIKeyServiceCreate*, TestProjectVariableService*, TestOrganizationVariableServicePatch*, TestServiceServiceCreate* parallel-induced flakes reproduce at HEAD without this change (22 failures with the file stashed; same set surfaces with the file in place; BE-0455's commit notes already documented this)."
